# oracle: fix rigid custom with fractional variable values: native casts them to integers by truncation (values 0.6, 0.7, 1.4, 1.45 make two bodies, not one), so f_1 has a second row
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 4.8e-16, atoms 0.0e+0. Before the fix the engine rounded the values and made one body (f_1[2][1]: rigid body 2 does not exist).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-12
units           lj
atom_modify     map array
region          box block 0 10 0 10 0 10
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 single 1 1 1
create_atoms    1 single 2 1 1
create_atoms    1 single 5 5 5
create_atoms    1 single 6 5 5
mass            1 1.0
variable        bid atom (id==1)*0.6+(id==2)*0.7+(id==3)*1.4+(id==4)*1.45
fix             1 all rigid custom v_bid
velocity        all set 0.1 0.2 -0.1 units box
pair_style      zero 2.0
pair_coeff      * *
timestep        0.005
thermo_style    custom step ke f_1[1][1] f_1[2][1] f_1[2][4]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             10
